{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>הכרת</b> — as is the way: for who throws upon a menstruant. The sense is that he says to the drunkards: how will you find wine, when <b>הכרת מנחה ונסך</b> — which is an obligation of the public. And he mentioned the grain offering, because grain was devastated; also the libation, if it is not found, it does not prevent [the offering]."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The comparison to a menstruant is left cryptic as per discipline; 'who throws upon' likely alludes to splashing/contamination, rendered literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:22.721193951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}